+/* Lazy regions (POSIX; -DGS_NO_LAZY_REGIONS for the eager ones): main's
+   regions are slots of one reservation that gs_rt_start makes for all of
+   them, PROT_NONE, so gs_reserve_region hands one out without a system
+   call. A slot's usable part becomes accessible on its first access, which
+   the fault handler turns into one mprotect (gs_lazy_enable) before the
+   access is retried; its guard gap stays PROT_NONE, as the eager gap is.
+   A region the program never touches then costs nothing, and one it does
+   one mprotect, where each used to cost an mmap and an mprotect at
+   start-up and two VMAs to tear down at exit.
+   GS_HOT_REGIONS, a list of registry indices (the order main reserves its
+   regions in), names the regions the program touches on nearly every run:
+   they take the first slots, next to each other, so that their first
+   pages share page-table pages, and are made accessible as they are
+   reserved, which costs less than the fault. It changes only where the
+   regions are and when they become accessible. */
